{"name":"Light Frosty Dawn","hex":"#d7efd5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"frosty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cold, chilly; icy.","Having frost on it or in it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frosty"},{"term":"dawn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To begin to brighten with daylight.","To start to appear or become obvious."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The morning twilight period immediately before sunrise.","The rising of the sun."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dawn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dawn","blocks":[{"text":"Dawn is the time that marks the beginning of twilight before sunrise. It is recognized by the appearance of indirect daylight being scattered in Earth's atmosphere, when the centre of the Sun's disc has reached 18° below the observer's horizon. This morning twilight period will last until sunrise, when direct daylight outshines the diffused light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Desert_Dawn.jpg/330px-Desert_Dawn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dawn","wikidata":"Q11326182"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg/500px-New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg/1280px-New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg/500px-New_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dawn at La Silla Observatory, Chile[4]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANew_Dawn_at_La_Silla.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg/500px-Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg/1280px-Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg/500px-Amanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dawn over Serra dos Órgãos National Park, Rio de Janeiro state, Brazil","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmanhecer_nos_Portais.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/L%27Aurore_by_William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_-_BMA.jpg/60px-L%27Aurore_by_William-Adolphe_Bouguerea